{
 "_meta": {
  "description": "NBA franchise colorways by era, post-1976 merger. For rendering generic era-accurate jerseys (no logos, no wordmarks). Years are season START years (e.g. 1995 = the 1995-96 season). Generated from general knowledge — every entry has a confidence flag. VERIFY all 'low' entries against teamcolorcodes.com and Basketball-Reference season pages before launch; transition years may be off by a season.",
  "fields": {
   "key": "unique id: TRICODE_startyear",
   "primary": "main jersey body color (road jersey base)",
   "secondary": "secondary/accent color",
   "trim": "trim/outline color",
   "eraStyle": "silhouette hint for renderer: classic (short/tight 70s-80s), nineties (looser, bold trim), baggy (2000s), modern (2010s+ minimal)",
   "confidence": "high | medium | low"
  },
  "relocations": "Franchises keyed by MODERN tricode. Historical identities (SEA, NJN, VAN, NOH, KC Kings, San Diego Clippers, Washington Bullets, Charlotte original Hornets) are separate era entries under the modern franchise with a 'identity' label so the renderer can note era city if you ever want it.",
  "aba": "ABA seasons (1967-1975 start years) are included so pre-merger careers render. Surviving franchises carry their ABA years under the modern key (IND/BKN/DEN/SAS); defunct clubs get their own keys (OAK, WSC, VIR, KEN, UTS, SPI, CAR, MMP, PIT, FLA, SDA, ANA, MNM, NOB, HSM). Colours are from the Wikipedia team infoboxes; VERIFY against bballjerseys.com/aba-* before launch — the ABA is the least reliable data in this file."
 },
